# Story 5: Tabs and Panes (50s)
# Hook: Tabs hold panes. Panes hold agents. It's that simple.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-05-tabs-and-panes.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 11

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Tabs hold panes. Panes hold agents. It's that simple.

[00:03.0 --> 00:06.0]
When you start rysh, you get one tab with one pane.

[00:06.0 --> 00:10.0]
Ctrl+T enters tab mode. Press n to create a new tab.

[00:10.0 --> 00:15.0]
Square brackets switch tabs. Left bracket goes back, right bracket goes forward.

[00:18.0 --> 00:23.0]
Ctrl+P enters pane mode. Press n to split right -- a new pane in a new column.

[00:23.0 --> 00:29.0]
The Tab key cycles between panes. Watch the border highlight change.

[00:29.0 --> 00:35.0]
Now you've got two panes side by side. Each one is an independent terminal.

[00:35.0 --> 00:38.0]
Alt plus arrow keys navigate globally. Alt Left/Right switches tabs.

[00:38.0 --> 00:42.0]
Tab key cycles between panes in the active tab.

[00:42.0 --> 00:46.0]
Mix and match. Each tab is an independent workspace.

[00:46.0 --> 00:50.0]
Tabs organize your workspace. Each pane is an independent terminal with its own shell and AI agent.

